From 8b850a18816e00d4ae1757c1de70b59e67cf3b84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:38:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(ui): WCS page applies its origin from the footer
 beside Close, and says where the origin is

The WCS page's Set origin moves from the page body, among the quarter
turns, to the fixed footer beside Close (egui_app::wcs_footer). While the
typed fields differ from the placed WCS, the footer shows "Origin not
applied". Positions are compared to 1e-9 mm and angles as rotations.

A new app::setup_origin says where the origin is, against the stock box
(else the model's bounds): "top of stock, front-left corner", or signed
distances from the box's left side, front and top when it is on none of
the 27 anchor points. The page's header line and the setup sheet's new
origin: line both read it.

docs/user-guide/work-origin.md explains where CamCraft shows the origin
and how to change it.

Fixes #870

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
